From feaba306eb0cd493a3ce92ccdb7630de470f10c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 02:40:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Review C1/C2: candidate configuration found; four defects in
 my own helper

THE 2x2 IS COMPLETE AND THE EFFECTS ARE ADDITIVE. shore all-gear across
daily+NB2 / weekly+NB2 / daily+ZINB / weekly+ZINB is 20,898 / 21,547 /
20,745 / 21,489: an interaction of +95 crab on a 21,500 component. The AR
resolution does all the work on p_loo and coverage (0.352 -> 0.095, cov50
dev 0.204 -> 0.069); the ZINB does the rest on the Pareto diagnostics
(41 -> 26 at daily, 1 -> 0 at weekly). C1 is the only fit in this project
with ZERO Pareto k above 0.7. Port total 72,032 [53,044, 101,212], +0.73%
on the current authoritative 71,513.

A CORRECTION CARRIED SINCE 2026-08-31. I repeatedly framed the shore
all-gear AR as bracketed by two bad ends, daily at coverage_50 0.701
(+7.1 SD) and monthly at 0.035 (-16.4 SD). The monthly figure is from the
GEAR-RESOLVED model, a different likelihood. The pooled bracket is daily
0.7010 (+7.1 SD), weekly 0.5659 (+2.3), biweekly 0.5659 (+2.3), monthly
0.5788 (+2.8): ONLY DAILY IS AN OUTLIER, and the three coarse rungs span
3.6% in catch. The evidence does not choose among them; the agreed rule
does, selecting weekly, and it is defensible because weekly is adequate on
every statistic rather than merely passing a gate everything passes.

THE ZINB, COMPARED LIKE FOR LIKE AT LAST. C1 vs L1 is same resolution,
same data, one likelihood difference: zero bin z +3.7 -> +2.0 and one bin
z -6.1 -> -3.3 on all-gear, both CLOSING on the pot-closure replicate
(+2.9 -> +0.7, -3.5 -> -1.2). elpd +11.6 at 2.30 paired SE, down from 2.69
at daily, which is the right direction: not an artefact of the overfitted
effort process. The all-gear one bin does not close; the data is more
bimodal than a zero-inflated NB can be and a hurdle model is the shape
that fits it, with the remaining gain bounded at ~6% of the catch.

FOUR DEFECTS, ALL IN CODE FROM THE PREVIOUS PATCH.
- bss_rung_adequacy() reported p_loo_frac as the sum over streams / summed
  n_obs, where bss_model_adequacy.R reports the WORST stream's fraction.
  One run printed 2.8% and 9.6% for the same fit. Fixed, verified.
- It called bss_ppc_calibration(), which reseeds, from inside the fitting
  loop. C2's kept fit is BIT-IDENTICAL to L1's across 10,251 parameter
  rows and still reported gear coverage_50 0.5659 against 0.5595: a
  diagnostic-only toggle moved a committed diagnostic. .Random.seed is now
  saved and restored.
- verdict_L1(dirs$C2) filed C2's rows under the L1 label, and
  merge_csv_by() de-duplicated only against the OLD file, so the verdicts
  carried two rows per criterion. Both fixed; the file is relabelled and
  annotated (those rungs carry the superseded p_loo definition and the RNG
  shift and cannot be recomputed from what was written).
- DRY_RUN <- FALSE committed for the fourth time. Reset.

RECOMMENDATION: adopt C1 via ar_max_resolution$pooled$shore$all_gear =
"weekly" and estimate_catch_zi = TRUE. C1 reached weekly through ar_force,
an experiment lever that bypasses the cap; production must route it
through the cap, which is one line and needs one confirming render gated
on reproducing C1 bit-identically.

Harness 372 -> 378.

